---
import '../styles/global.css';

interface Props {
	title: string;
}
const { title } = Astro.props;
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
		<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-L9MXJPQ4BW"></script>
		<script is:inline>
		  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
		  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
		  gtag('js', new Date());
		  gtag('config', 'G-L9MXJPQ4BW');
		</script>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
		<title>{title}</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Boto Tracks: The definitive AWS Boto3 and Botocore changelog tracker. Search, filter, and track every AWS SDK update, fix, and feature in real-time. Learn how to track boto changes efficiently." />
		<meta name="keywords" content="boto tracks, boto-tracks, aws boto tracks, aws sdk python, botocore changelog, boto3 updates, aws sdk tracker, python aws development, botocore intelligence, boto3 release notes, aws changelog, how to track boto changes" />
		<meta name="author" content="Tunaxia" />
		
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0a0a" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
		<meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />
		<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent" />
		
		<!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:title" content="Boto Tracks | AWS Boto3 & Botocore Intelligence Tracker" />
		<meta property="og:description" content="The ultimate platform for AWS Boto3 and Botocore updates. Search and track every AWS SDK for Python change in real-time." />
		<meta property="og:url" content="https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/" />
		<meta property="og:image" content="https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/favicon.png" />

		<!-- Twitter -->
		<meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<meta property="twitter:title" content="Boto Tracks | AWS Boto3 & Botocore Intelligence Tracker" />
		<meta property="twitter:description" content="Search and filter every update in the Boto ecosystem. Track AWS SDK changes with ease." />
		<meta property="twitter:image" content="https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/favicon.png" />

		<link rel="canonical" href="https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
		<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/favicon.png" />

		<script is:inline>
			(function() {
				const setTheme = () => {
					const darkMode = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
					document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', darkMode);
				};
				setTheme();
				window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').addEventListener('change', setTheme);
			})();
		</script>

		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@400;600;900&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" media="print" onload="this.media='all'" />
		
		<script type="application/ld+json">
		{
		  "@context": "https://schema.org",
		  "@graph": [
			{
			  "@type": "WebSite",
			  "@id": "https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/#website",
			  "url": "https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/",
			  "name": "Boto Tracks",
			  "publisher": { "@id": "https://tunaxia.com/#organization" },
			  "description": "Modern AWS Boto3 & Botocore changelog tracker and intelligence platform."
			},
			{
			  "@type": "Organization",
			  "@id": "https://tunaxia.com/#organization",
			  "name": "Tunaxia",
			  "url": "https://tunaxia.com/",
			  "logo": "https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/favicon.png",
			  "sameAs": [
				"https://github.com/tunaxia"
			  ]
			},
			{
			  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
			  "@id": "https://boto-tracks.tunaxia.com/#software",
			  "name": "Boto Tracks",
			  "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
			  "operatingSystem": "Web",
			  "author": { "@id": "https://tunaxia.com/#organization" },
			  "description": "A high-performance interface for tracking AWS Boto3 and Botocore changelogs, developed by Tunaxia."
			},
			{
			  "@type": "FAQPage",
			  "mainEntity": [
				{
				  "@type": "Question",
				  "name": "What is Boto Tracks?",
				  "acceptedAnswer": {
					"@type": "Answer",
					"text": "Boto Tracks is the definitive intelligence platform for tracking and searching changes in the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3 and Botocore). It provides a real-time searchable timeline of all AWS updates."
				  }
				},
				{
				  "@type": "Question",
				  "name": "How to track boto changes?",
				  "acceptedAnswer": {
					"@type": "Answer",
					"text": "You can track Boto changes using Boto Tracks. It provides a comprehensive dashboard to filter updates by AWS service (like S3, EC2, Lambda) and release version, making it easy to see exactly what changed in the AWS SDK for Python."
				  }
				},
				{
				  "@type": "Question",
				  "name": "What are AWS Boto Tracks?",
				  "acceptedAnswer": {
					"@type": "Answer",
					"text": "AWS Boto Tracks refers to the historical tracking of releases and updates for the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3 and Botocore). This includes tracking new features, API changes, and bug fixes across all AWS services."
				  }
				}
			  ]
			}
		  ]
		}
		</script>
	</head>
	<body class="h-screen w-full overflow-hidden bg-main transition-colors duration-500">
		<slot />

		<!-- SEO hidden hooks -->
		<footer class="sr-only">
			<section>
				<h2>Boto Tracks | AWS Boto3 & Botocore Changelog Tracker</h2>
				<p>
					Boto Tracks is the definitive intelligence platform for tracking <strong>AWS Boto Tracks</strong>, <strong>AWS Botocore</strong>, and <strong>Boto3</strong> changelogs. 
					Developed by <strong>Tunaxia</strong>, it provides a searchable, filterable timeline 
					of every AWS SDK for Python release.
				</p>
				<h3>How to track Boto changes effectively?</h3>
				<p>
					Stay ahead of cloud infrastructure changes with <strong>Boto Tracks</strong>. 
					Whether you are looking for <strong>S3 API changes</strong>, <strong>EC2 bug fixes</strong>, or <strong>Lambda feature releases</strong>, 
					Boto Tracks provides the most efficient developer interface to track AWS SDK updates.
				</p>
				<h3>Key Features of Boto Tracks</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>AWS Boto Tracks Search:</strong> Query thousands of AWS service updates in milliseconds.</li>
					<li><strong>Boto-Tracks Intelligence:</strong> Quickly isolate new capabilities and API enhancements.</li>
					<li><strong>Fix Tracking:</strong> Identify critical patches and security updates in Boto3 and Botocore.</li>
					<li><strong>Service History:</strong> Deep-dive into the evolution of specific AWS SDK components.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>Optimize your AWS development workflow with the ultimate <strong>Boto3 release tracker</strong>. Built by developers at <a href="https://tunaxia.com" aria-label="Visit Tunaxia's official website">Tunaxia</a>.</p>
			</section>
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>